/-!
# CBSTM03B → Rust: the generated statement of one call

Generated by `tools/modernize/genstmt.py --subprogram` from veriforch's `mapping.json`, coblean's IR
and coblean's per-call theorem `cbstm03b_call`; do not edit.  CBSTM03B is a CALLed subprogram whose
storage and files persist from one call to the next, so the statement is about one call: for every
callee state and parameter area allowed by coblean's theorem (its binders and hypotheses, copied from
its source) and every translation state related to them, the call of the translation and the COBOL
run correspond, and their results are related in the same way.  The relations, all generated:
* one per file: the open flag, the records (each decoding to the struct / object field values), the
  read position and the end-of-file flag of coblean's file state (the last record read, `cur`, is
  not part of it);
* `StateRel` (the state kept between calls): the files, the FD record areas and the FILE STATUS
  items, at their storage offsets;
* one per parameter area (linkage item): its field values at its storage offsets;
* `EnvRel`: the environment's outcome of `OPEN INPUT` for each file (none, or a failure status);
* `Rel`: the call returns (no exception / panic) and the COBOL run ends with GOBACK, in related states.

The inputs are restricted to the domain `EquivLean.Modernize.Cbstm03b.Domain`, written by hand in `EquivLean.Modernize.Cbstm03b.Domain`
(the one part of the statement not generated).
-/

